{"availability":"available","full":"kvantixtech/weather-forecast-test","name":"weather-forecast-test","description":"Which weather forecast is right most often in Denmark? DMI, MET Norway, OpenWeatherMap and TAF, locked before the weather happens.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-28T07:54:42Z","updated":"2026-10-10T04:21:57Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://kvantix.tech/playground/","topics":["denmark","dmi","forecast-verification","forecasting","hash-chain","open-data","reproducible-research","weather"],"demo":"https://kvantix.tech/playground/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T19:00:17.194Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T19:00:17.194Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T19:00:17.194Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T07:35:11.324Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T19:00:17.194Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Which weather forecast is right most often in Denmark?","This collector saves what DMI, MET Norway, OpenWeatherMap (free 3-hour forecast) and the pilots' airport forecast (TAF) predict for five Danish cities, four times a day. It locks every download in a SHA-256 hash chain before the weather happens. Afterwards it fetches what DMI's weather stations actually measured and scores every source against it, and against a lazy baseline: \"tomorrow will be like today\".","The scoring rules in this repository were fixed and published before the first forecast was collected. The commit history is the proof."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kvantixtech/weather-forecast-test/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d0a8e6ef881f1383149697393aac07e0a016dd89cadb54adc7193a65dac5fe6d","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:11.806Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:11.806Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Which weather forecast is right most often in Denmark?","sourceUrl":"https://github